      "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b",
      "decision": "answerable",
      "answer": "ColBERT reduces the space footprint of its index by applying a form of vector‑quantization: each document embedding is split into a number of sub‑vectors (for example, s = 16) and each sub‑vector is stored as a single byte. The index then performs similarity computations directly in this compressed byte‑domain, which both cuts the memory required to hold the index and speeds up search. No residual‑compression technique is described in the provided passages.",
      "verified_claims": [
        {
          "claim_text": "ColBERT reduces the space footprint of its index by applying a form of vector‑quantization: each document embedding is split into a number of sub‑vectors (for example, s = 16) and each sub‑vector is stored as a single byte.",
          "citation_chunk_id": "khattab-2020-colbert:ck256:p6:c44",
          "doc_id": "khattab-2020-colbert",
          "page": 6,
          "evidence_quote": "To improve memory efficiency, every embedding is divided into s (e.g., s = 16) sub-vectors, each represented using one byte."
        },
        {
          "claim_text": "The index then performs similarity computations directly in this compressed byte‑domain, which both cuts the memory required to hold the index and speeds up search.",
          "citation_chunk_id": "khattab-2020-colbert:ck256:p6:c44",
          "doc_id": "khattab-2020-colbert",
          "page": 6,
          "evidence_quote": "Moreover, the index conducts the similarity computations in this compressed domain, leading to cheaper computations and thus faster search."
        }
      ],
