    "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b",
    "decision": "answerable",
    "answer": "REALM (Guu et al., 2020) trains its dense retriever jointly with the language model in an end‑to‑end fashion, optimizing the retriever together with the downstream task loss (cross‑entropy). In contrast, RAG (Lewis et al., 2020) adopts the DPR dense retriever, which is pre‑trained separately using a contrastive loss that aligns query and passage embeddings, and the retriever is trained in isolation of the downstream task before being plugged into the generation model.",
    "verified_claims": [
      {
        "claim_text": "REALM trains its dense retriever end‑to‑end with the downstream task to maximize the final training cross‑entropy.",
        "citation_chunk_id": "borgeaud-2022-retro:ck256:p9:c43",
        "doc_id": "borgeaud-2022-retro",
        "page": 9,
        "evidence_quote": "This potential issue is specifically addressed by Realm (Guu et al., 2020), which trains the retrieval system end-to-end to maximize the final training cross-entropy."
      }
    ],
